{
  "name": "What maintenance tasks should seniors prioritize?",
  "step": [
    {
      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "When it comes to senior home maintenance, prioritizing tasks is all about safety and ease of use. First up, focus on fall prevention. This means regularly checking for and securing any loose rugs, or better yet, removing them if they're not essential. Keep walkways clear of clutter and make sure there's good lighting, especially in transition areas like hallways, stairs, and entryways. Next, pay attention to entry and exit points – are doors easy to open and close? Are thresholds causing a tripping hazard? It’s also super important to keep frequently used items within easy reach to avoid unnecessary bending or stretching. Don't forget bathroom safety; checking grab bars, ensuring non-slip surfaces, and making sure the toilet and shower are accessible are critical. Postponing small repairs can turn them into bigger hazards down the line, so tackle them promptly. If you're not sure where to start or need a hand with some of these tasks, HH Remodeling LLC offers handyman services that can help keep your home safe and functional. Give us a call at 303-505-0866 to discuss your home maintenance needs.",
      "@type": "HowToStep",
      "position": 1
    }
  ],
